@@ -53,3 +53,7 @@ Any OIDC-compliant provider works, inclu
 <Callout type="info">
 LearnHouse uses OIDC Discovery to find the authorization, token and userinfo endpoints from the issuer URL. Make sure your identity provider exposes a `/.well-known/openid-configuration` document.
 </Callout>
+
+## Self-hosted identity providers
+
+LearnHouse reaches the identity provider over `https://` only, and refuses private and internal addresses so an issuer URL cannot be pointed at the instance's own network. If your provider runs on a private address, list its hostname in `LEARNHOUSE_SSO_TRUSTED_HOSTS` on the API (comma-separated, for example `auth.example.com`). Only SSO requests to those hosts skip the address check.
